{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1147605-help-converting-masquerade-ideas-to-a-requiem-game","id":1147605,"title":"Help converting masquerade ideas to a requiem game","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-10-06T16:09:57-07:00","id":1147605,"title":"Help converting masquerade ideas to a requiem game","content":"So i want to give running something a go, and i love both vtm and vtr, now i would much rather run requiem, largely for mechanical reasons, but there are some things that i want to use from masquerade that don't have a equivalent in requiem.<br /> I really like the idea of having the PCs being Caitif - not a thing in Requiem<br /> i also want to use masquerade Revenants (particularly the Enrathi and Rafastio) as antagonists (or at least the minions of the antagonists)<br /> <br /> now short of converting these things across what can i do, is their anything i could use instead?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12845-ahather","name":"ahather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12845_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-06T16:24:13-07:00","id":1147608,"title":"","content":"Revenants have an equivalent in ghoul families. <br /> <br /> Caitiff have an equivalent in, confusingly enough, revenants. Although if you wanted to make them more like the masquerade version you could chop out all the major downsides and just make them clanless full vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-06T17:52:24-07:00","id":1147622,"title":"","content":"Danse Macabre has some advice for looser Clans that would work well for Caitiff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-06T18:13:51-07:00","id":1147630,"title":"","content":"The Vampire Translation Guide suggests these mechanics for converting Caitiff over.<br /> <br /> 'Systems: Caitiff don\u2019t have a clan weakness, but that\u2019s not to say that they don\u2019t have their own afflictions. Their blood is weak. Spend a point of Vitae boosts a Caitiff\u2019s Physical Attribute by one, not two (see p. 157 of Vampire: The Requiem). In addition, the vampire purchases all Disciplines as though they were &quot;out of clan&quot; (new dots x 7). The player can choose one &quot;affinity&quot; Discipline for the character; this Discipline costs (new dots x 6) to raise. Caitiff aren\u2019t explicitly barred from membership in covenants, but they have a harder time becoming accepted \u2014 the Status (City) and Status (Covenant) Merits cost (new dots x 3). Status (Clan) is banned. <br /> Caitiff characters do not receive favored Attributes.'<br /> <br /> It's based on first edition so the Experiences are different.<br /> <br /> Revenants can probably just be ghouls that produce their own Vitae, though for the Rafastio you might make them Proximi, from Mage the Awakening, in addition to ghouls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-07T03:58:04-07:00","id":1147724,"title":"","content":"thanks for the Proximi idea, I might have to use that, going to wait for Half Damned, to work out the details of revenants (probs using ghoul families that don't need a vampire.)<br /> <br /> On Caitif: thinking about it i can just come up with another reason why there is pressure for the prince to have the PCs executed","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12845-ahather","name":"ahather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12845_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-07T06:43:45-07:00","id":1147749,"title":"","content":"If you also want to emphasize the &quot;Weak Blood&quot; theme of Caitiff. Let Blood Potency appears as 1 level lower than usual. Be it as the Benefits to rage, or resisting and Aura effect to adopting a blood line, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Gamelines: Requiem, Lost, Awakening, Trinity Continuum: Aeon, some V5.<br /> Likes cheesecake (quark-based)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1305-maekkel","name":"maekkel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1305_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-07T11:13:29-07:00","id":1147829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ahather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1147605-help-converting-masquerade-ideas-to-a-requiem-game?p=1147724#post1147724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On Caitif: thinking about it i can just come up with another reason why there is pressure for the prince to have the PCs executed</div> </div> </div> </div>You could also make them Neglatu (if they don't care about bloodline). Or make their sire a Strix instead of another Kindred.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}